    "title": "'Song Sung Blue's' Kate Hudson loses out to 'Hamnet's' Jessie Buckley for best actress Oscar",
    "text": "March 15, 2026, 10:07 p.m. CTJessie Buckley won the Academy Award for best actress in a leading role for her portrayal of William Shakespeare's wife, Agnes, in \"Hamnet.\"That meant a loss for Kate Hudson, who was also nominated in the best actress category, for her portrayal of Milwaukee's own Claire Sardina in \"Song Sung Blue.\" The biopic is about Claire and her late husband, Mike (played by Hugh Jackman) – the real-life couple behind the Neil Diamond tribute band Lightning & Thunder. The movie is based on a 2008 documentary about the duo, also called \"Song Sung Blue.\"While \"Blue\" had made the Oscars shortlist for cinematography, it ultimately wasn't one of the final five nominees.The other best actress nominees were Rose Byrne (\"If I Had Legs I'd Kick You\"), Renate Reinsve (\"Sentimental Value\") and Emma Stone (\"Bugonia\").The 98th Academy Awards were held Sunday, March 15, at the Dolby Theatre at Ovation Hollywood. It was a mother-daughter date night for Hudson and her mom, fellow actress Goldie Hawn. Hawn has received two Oscar nominations throughout her career, winning one.Hudson's only other Oscar nomination thus far came 2½ decades ago for best supporting actress for her role as Penny Lane in \"Almost Famous.\"",
